From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: stay awake for a while after crash recovery

Once crash recovery has finished, the system may suspend at once; on
Android it did so 3 ms after the recovery. With WoWLAN the WoW suspend
then runs on firmware that has only just restarted and isn't connected
yet, and on a WCN6855 that crashed the firmware again, recovery after
recovery: 478 crashes in three hours.

Keep the recovery wakeup source for ATH11K_RECOVERY_SETTLE_MS (10 s)
after a successful recovery. This also gives the connection time to
come back before the system sleeps.

Tested-on: WCN6855 hw2.1 PCI WLAN.HSP.1.1-03125-QCAHSPSWPL_V1_V2_SILICONZ_LITE-3.6510.41

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h | 1 +
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c  | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
index 49e032f75..cdc5816ca 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/core.h
@@ -72,6 +72,7 @@ extern bool ath11k_ftm_mode;
 #define ATH11K_RECONFIGURE_TIMEOUT_HZ (10 * HZ)
 #define ATH11K_RECOVER_START_TIMEOUT_HZ (20 * HZ)
 #define ATH11K_RECOVERY_WAKEUP_MS (60 * MSEC_PER_SEC)
+#define ATH11K_RECOVERY_SETTLE_MS (10 * MSEC_PER_SEC)
 
 enum ath11k_supported_bw {
 	ATH11K_BW_20	= 0,
diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
index 3360299fc..8b8c3eb58 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/mac.c
@@ -9293,7 +9293,14 @@ ath11k_mac_op_reconfig_complete(struct ieee80211_hw *hw,
 				complete(&ab->reset_complete);
 				ab->is_reset = false;
 				atomic_set(&ab->fail_cont_count, 0);
+				/*
+				 * Stay awake a little longer: WoW on firmware
+				 * that has only just restarted crashes it again,
+				 * and the connection needs a moment to return.
+				 */
 				__pm_relax(ab->recovery_ws);
+				pm_wakeup_ws_event(ab->recovery_ws,
+						   ATH11K_RECOVERY_SETTLE_MS, false);
 				ath11k_dbg(ab, ATH11K_DBG_BOOT, "reset success\n");
 			}
 		}
